<h3 dir=3D"ltr" id=3D"2.-accepting-loose-types-&lt;span">2. Accepting loose=
 types</h3>
<p dir=3D"ltr" class=3D"p-margin"><span style=3D"background-color: transpar=
ent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decor=
ation: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Injection vu=
lnerabilities frequently arise when APIs accept overly permissive data type=
s like </span><span style=3D"background-color: transparent; font-weight: bo=
ld; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertic=
al-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">interface{}</span><span style=
=3D"background-color: transparent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; fo=
nt-variant: normal; text-decoration: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-=
space: pre-wrap;"> or generic maps. These flexible structures can harbor em=
bedded MongoDB operators or malicious object constructs that bypass intende=
d query logic.</span></p>
<p dir=3D"ltr" class=3D"p-margin"><span style=3D"background-color: transpar=
ent; font-weight: 400; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-decor=
ation: none; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;">Minimize use=
 of loose tying unless absolutely essential and implement strict validation=
 when unavoidable. Instead, define explicit data structures that match your=
 expected input format and constraint acceptable values.</span></p>
